# SOLID Principles Anti-Patterns

Violations of SOLID principles and dependency management.

---

## 1. Coupling Redux to Domain

**Context:** When Domain layer knows about Redux or global state. Domain must remain pure and independent.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Domain importing Redux types
// src/domain/usecases/vaga/ListarVagasUseCase.ts
import { RootState } from '@/app/store'; // Domain knows Redux!

@injectable()
export class ListarVagasUseCase {
  execute(state: RootState): Vaga[] { // Depends on Redux state shape
    const filtros = state.vaga.filtros;
    // ...
  }
}

// ❌ BAD: Domain using Redux hooks
// src/domain/entities/Feedback.ts
import { useSelector } from 'react-redux'; // Domain knows React-Redux!

export class Feedback {
  get usuarioAtual(): Usuario {
    return useSelector(state => state.auth.usuario); // Direct Redux access!
  }
}

// ❌ BAD: Domain importing store
// src/domain/services/NotificacaoService.ts
import { store } from '@/app/store'; // Domain knows store!

export class NotificacaoService {
  enviar(notificacao: Notificacao): void {
    const usuario = store.getState().auth.usuario; // Direct store access!
    // ...
  }
}
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Domain receives dependencies via injection
// src/domain/usecases/vaga/ListarVagasUseCase.ts
export interface FiltroVaga {
  status?: StatusVaga;
  dataInicio?: Date;
  dataFim?: Date;
}

@injectable()
export class ListarVagasUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('VagaRepository') private repo: VagaRepository
  ) {}
  
  async execute(filtro: FiltroVaga): Promise<Vaga[]> {
    // Pure domain logic, no Redux dependency
    return this.repo.listar(filtro);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Current user passed as parameter
// src/domain/services/NotificacaoService.ts
@injectable()
export class NotificacaoService {
  constructor(
    @inject('EmailProvider') private email: EmailProvider,
    @inject('PushProvider') private push: PushProvider
  ) {}
  
  async enviar(
    notificacao: Notificacao,
    destinatario: Usuario // Passed as parameter, not from global state
  ): Promise<void> {
    await Promise.all([
      this.email.enviar(destinatario.email, notificacao),
      this.push.enviar(destinatario.id, notificacao)
    ]);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: App layer bridges Redux and Domain
// src/app/store/vagaThunks.ts
export const listarVagas = createAsyncThunk(
  'vaga/listar',
  async (_, { getState, rejectWithValue }) => {
    const container = getContainer();
    const useCase = container.resolve(ListarVagasUseCase);
    
    // Extract filter from Redux state here in App layer
    const { filtros } = getState().vaga;
    
    // Pass as plain DTO to domain
    const filtroDTO: FiltroVaga = {
      status: filtros.status,
      dataInicio: filtros.dataInicio ? new Date(filtros.dataInicio) : undefined,
      dataFim: filtros.dataFim ? new Date(filtros.dataFim) : undefined
    };
    
    try {
      const vagas = await useCase.execute(filtroDTO);
      return vagas;
    } catch (error) {
      return rejectWithValue(error.message);
    }
  }
);
```

**Layer Boundaries:**

| Layer | Can Know About | Must NOT Know About |
|-------|----------------|---------------------|
| Domain | Shared types, domain interfaces | Redux, React, store, global state |
| App | Domain, Redux | Presentation components |
| Presentation | App (Redux), Domain types | Domain implementation details |

**Impact:**

- Reuse impossibility - domain tied to specific app state shape
- Fragile tests - need Redux store to test domain logic
- Testing difficulty - can't test UseCase without mocking store
- Architecture violation - breaks Clean Architecture principles

**Detection:**

- `import { useSelector }` in `domain/` files
- `import { store }` in `domain/` files
- `import { RootState }` in `domain/` files
- `getState()` calls outside of thunks/middleware
- Check: `grep -r "from '@reduxjs\/toolkit'\|from 'react-redux'" src/domain/`

**Architecture Reference:**

See `@ARCHITECTURE.md` Section 5: "Domain nao deve conhecer estado global (Redux)."

