## 2. Direct Instantiation (Breaking Dependency Inversion)

**Context:** When classes create their own dependencies instead of receiving them. Violates Dependency Inversion Principle.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Class creates its own dependencies
// src/domain/usecases/feedback/EnviarFeedbackUseCase.ts
export class EnviarFeedbackUseCase {
  private repository: FeedbackRepository;
  private notificador: EmailService;
  
  constructor() {
    // Direct instantiation!
    this.repository = new FeedbackRepositoryImpl();
    this.notificador = new EmailService(); // Depends on concrete implementation
  }
  
  async execute(dados: FeedbackDTO): Promise<void> {
    await this.repository.salvar(dados);
    await this.notificador.enviar(dados);
  }
}

// ❌ BAD: new keyword in method
// src/domain/services/RelatorioService.ts
export class RelatorioService {
  async gerarRelatorio(dados: DadosRelatorio): Promise<Buffer> {
    const gerador = new PdfGenerator(); // Direct instantiation in method!
    return gerador.gerar(dados);
  }
}

// ❌ BAD: Factory with hardcoded implementation
// src/data/api/ApiFactory.ts
export class ApiFactory {
  static createUsuarioApi(): UsuarioApi {
    return new UsuarioApiImpl(); // Hardcoded concrete class
  }
}
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Dependencies injected via constructor
// src/domain/usecases/feedback/EnviarFeedbackUseCase.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';

@injectable()
export class EnviarFeedbackUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('FeedbackRepository') 
    private repository: FeedbackRepository, // Interface, not concrete
    
    @inject('NotificacaoService') 
    private notificador: NotificacaoService // Interface, not concrete
  ) {}
  
  async execute(dados: FeedbackDTO): Promise<Resultado<Feedback>> {
    const feedback = new Feedback(dados);
    
    await this.repository.salvar(feedback);
    await this.notificador.enviar(feedback);
    
    return { sucesso: true, dados: feedback };
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Dependency passed as parameter
// src/domain/services/RelatorioService.ts
@injectable()
export class RelatorioService {
  constructor(
    @inject('PdfGenerator') private pdfGenerator: PdfGenerator
  ) {}
  
  async gerarRelatorio(dados: DadosRelatorio): Promise<Buffer> {
    // Uses injected dependency, doesn't create it
    return this.pdfGenerator.gerar(dados);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Container resolves dependencies
// src/core/di/container.ts
import { container } from 'tsyringe';
import { UsuarioRepositoryImpl } from '@/data/repositories/UsuarioRepositoryImpl';
import { UsuarioApi } from '@/data/api/UsuarioApi';

// Register implementations
container.register('UsuarioRepository', {
  useClass: UsuarioRepositoryImpl
});

container.register('UsuarioApi', {
  useValue: usuarioApi
});

// Usage in component/page
// src/presentation/pages/Perfil.tsx
const PerfilPage = () => {
  const container = useContainer();
  const obterUsuarioUseCase = container.resolve(ObterUsuarioUseCase);
  // Container injects all dependencies automatically
};
```

**Dependency Inversion Principle:**

| Violation | Solution |
|-----------|----------|
| `new ConcreteClass()` | Constructor injection |
| Direct instantiation | DI container resolution |
| Hardcoded dependencies | Interface abstraction |
| `import { Impl } from '...'` | `import { Interface } from '@/domain/...'` |

**Impact:**

- Low test coverage - can't mock dependencies
- High fragility - changing implementation breaks tests
- Tight coupling - modules depend on concrete implementations
- No flexibility - can't swap implementations (e.g., mock for testing)

**Detection:**

- `new` keyword in domain/usecase files (outside of factory methods)
- Concrete class imports in domain: `import { RepoImpl }`
- Constructor calling `new` to create dependencies
- Hardcoded class names in "factory" functions

**Testability Comparison:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Hard to test - uses real repository
class BadUseCase {
  private repo = new VagaRepositoryImpl(); // Real API calls!
}

// ✅ GOOD: Easy to test - can inject mock
class GoodUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('VagaRepository') private repo: VagaRepository
  ) {}
}

// Test:
const mockRepo = { listar: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue([]) };
const useCase = new GoodUseCase(mockRepo);
```

**Architecture Reference:**

See `@ARCHITECTURE.md` Section 6: "DI Container (TSyringe) - injetar dependencias via construtor."

