## 5. Open/Closed Principle Violations
n**Context:** When modifying existing code to add new features instead of extending. Open for extension, closed for modification.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Adding cases to existing switch
// src/domain/services/CalculadoraSalario.ts
export class CalculadoraSalario {
  calcular(valor: number, tipo: TipoContrato): number {
    switch (tipo) {
      case 'CLT':
        return valor * 1.3;
      case 'PJ':
        return valor;
      case 'ESTAGIO': // Added later - modified existing class!
        return valor * 0.8;
      default:
        return valor;
    }
  }
}

// ❌ BAD: Modifying enum and all usages
// src/domain/enums/StatusCandidatura.ts
export enum StatusCandidatura {
  PENDENTE = 'PENDENTE',
  APROVADO = 'APROVADO',
  REPROVADO = 'REPROVADO',
  // Added later - must modify all switch statements!
  EM_ANALISE = 'EM_ANALISE'
}
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Strategy pattern for extensibility
// src/domain/strategies/SalarioStrategy.ts
export interface SalarioStrategy {
  calcular(valorBase: number): number;
}

@injectable()
export class CltStrategy implements SalarioStrategy {
  calcular(valorBase: number): number {
    return valorBase * 1.3;
  }
}

@injectable()
export class PjStrategy implements SalarioStrategy {
  calcular(valorBase: number): number {
    return valorBase;
  }
}

@injectable()
export class EstagioStrategy implements SalarioStrategy {
  calcular(valorBase: number): number {
    return valorBase * 0.8;
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Calculator uses strategy - open for extension
@injectable()
export class CalculadoraSalario {
  constructor(
    @injectAll('SalarioStrategy') 
    private strategies: Map<string, SalarioStrategy>
  ) {}
  
  calcular(valor: number, tipo: string): number {
    const strategy = this.strategies.get(tipo);
    if (!strategy) {
      throw new Error(`Tipo de contrato desconhecido: ${tipo}`);
    }
    return strategy.calcular(valor);
  }
}

// New contract type? Just add new strategy - no existing code modified!
```

**Impact:**

- Regression risk - every modification can break existing code
- Testing burden - must retest all existing functionality
- Code instability - frequent changes to stable classes
- Merge conflicts - multiple developers modifying same file

**Detection:**

- Frequent modifications to existing classes
- Adding cases to switch statements
- Modifying enums
- Comments like "added for feature X"
- Long methods with many conditionals

